# Per cell generator recipes (LAYER 3 knobs only, safe to vary per cell).
#
# These control lclayout's *algorithms*, not the process or library architecture.
# DRC rules, row height, site, routing tracks and unit_cell_width are NOT here:
# they live in tech/sky130_hd_tech.py and are identical for every cell, because
# cells must abut in rows and expose pins on common tracks. A cell being
# individually LVS clean is necessary but NOT sufficient, the library must be
# co legal, which is why the architecture is shared.
#
# Columns (whitespace separated):
#   cell           placer        router     mcon_weight  lift
#     cell        : short cell name (e.g. inv_1), or 'default'
#     placer      : meta | flat | hierarchical | smt
#     router      : dijkstra | steiner
#     mcon_weight : integer routing cost of the li1<->met1 via (RECIPE_MCON_WEIGHT)
#     lift        : 0/1 (RECIPE_LIFT_DRAINS), lift parallel signal (drain) diffusion
#                   contacts off the same polarity power rail so their li1 pad cannot
#                   abut/merge with the rail. Fixes the NOR/AOI parallel pulldown short.
#                   DEFAULT 0: only turn on for cells that actually short AND still
#                   route with it on. Forcing it on compound cells (and3/mux2/...)
#                   over constrains routing and makes them unroutable, so it is opt-in.
#                   (column optional; absent => 0)
#
# The 'default' row applies to any cell without its own line. A per cell line
# overrides the default for that cell. Environment variables (PLACER, ROUTER,
# RECIPE_MCON_WEIGHT, RECIPE_LIFT_DRAINS) passed to run_cell.sh still win.
#
# cell           placer         router     mcon_weight  lift
default          hierarchical   dijkstra   300000       0
